   </div></details></nav></div></header><script>(function(){var d=document.querySelector(".mnav");if(!d)return;document.addEventListener("click",function(e){if(d.open&&!d.contains(e.target))d.open=false});document.addEventListener("keydown",function(e){if(e.key==="Escape"&&d.open){d.open=false;d.querySelector("summary").focus()}})})();</script><main><nav class="crumb w" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › <a href="/nclex-practice-questions">Practice questions</a> › <span>Management of Care</span></nav><section class="hero w"><h1>Management of Care NCLEX Practice Questions</h1><p class="lead">The biggest NCLEX-RN category: 15–21% of the exam, about 1 in 5 questions. It's the "who goes first, who does what" side of nursing. Try 8 free questions below.</p>
      <div class="daily">Today's free NCLEX question is highlighted below. Come back tomorrow for a new one.</div><p><span class="pill moc-top">The largest NCLEX-RN category</span><span class="pill">15–21% of the NCLEX-RN</span><span class="pill">193 questions in Vexcura</span><span class="pill">Reviewed November 2026</span></p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/app#practice/MOC">Practice more Management of Care questions</a><a class="btn alt" href="/free-nclex-practice-exam">Take the full practice exam</a></div></section>
      <div class="w"><style>.moc-top{background:var(--gold);color:#fff;border-color:var(--gold)}.mocw{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:20px 22px;margin:8px 0 26px}.mocw h2{margin-top:0}.mbars{margin:14px 0 6px}.mb{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,15em) 1fr 4.2em;gap:10px;align-items:center;padding:5px 0;font-size:15px}.mb .mbn a{color:var(--ink)}.mbt{position:relative;height:14px;background:var(--sunk);border-radius:7px;overflow:hidden}.mbt i{position:absolute;top:0;bottom:0;background:var(--line)}.mbt i.lo{left:0;background:var(--muted);opacity:.55}.mb.me .mbt i{background:var(--gold);opacity:.45}.mb.me .mbt i.lo{background:var(--gold);opacity:1}.mb.me{font-weight:600}.mbv{text-align:right;white-space:nowrap;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--muted)}.mb.me .mbv{color:var(--ink)}.mocg{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(15em,1fr));gap:12px;margin:18px 0 4px}.mocg div{background:var(--bg);border-radius:10px;padding:12px 14px}.mocg b{display:block;font-size:17px;margin-bottom:4px}.mocg p{margin:0;font-size:15px}.mocf{border-left:4px solid var(--gold);background:var(--surface);padding:14px 18px;border-radius:0 10px 10px 0;margin:22px 0}.mocf h2{margin-top:0}.mocs{font-size:13.5px;color:var(--muted)}.mocs li{margin:3px 0}@media (max-width:560px){.mb{grid-template-columns:1fr auto;row-gap:5px;font-size:14px}.mb .mbt{grid-column:1/-1;grid-row:2}}</style><section class="mocw" id="why-it-matters"><h2>Why it matters most</h2><p>It has the highest share of all 8 categories, in both the 2023 and 2026 test plans<sup><a href="#moc-src-1">[1]</a></sup><sup><a href="#moc-src-2">[2]</a></sup>.</p><div class="mbars" role="img" aria-label="NCLEX-RN categories by share of the exam. Management of Care is the largest at 15 to 21 percent."><div class="mb me"><span class="mbn"><b>Management of Care</b></span><span class="mbt"><i style="left:71.4%;width:28.6%"></i><i class="lo" style="width:71.4%"></i></span><span class="mbv">15–21%</span></div><div class="mb"><span class="mbn"><a href="/nclex-practice-questions/pharmacology">Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies</a></span><span class="mbt"><i style="left:61.9%;width:28.6%"></i><i class="lo" style="width:61.9%"></i></span><span class="mbv">13–19%</span></div><div class="mb"><span class="mbn"><a href="/nclex-practice-questions/physiological-adaptation">Physiological Adaptation</a></span><span class="mbt"><i style="left:52.4%;width:28.6%"></i><i class="lo" style="width:52.4%"></i></span><span class="mbv">11–17%</span></div><div class="mb"><span class="mbn"><a href="/nclex-practice-questions/safety-and-infection-control">Safety and Infection Prevention and Control</a></span><span class="mbt"><i style="left:47.6%;width:28.6%"></i><i class="lo" style="width:47.6%"></i></span><span class="mbv">10–16%</span></div><div class="mb"><span class="mbn"><a href="/nclex-practice-questions/reduction-of-risk-potential">Reduction of Risk Potential</a></span><span class="mbt"><i style="left:42.9%;width:28.6%"></i><i class="lo" style="width:42.9%"></i></span><span class="mbv">9–15%</span></div><div class="mb"><span class="mbn"><a href="/nclex-practice-questions/health-promotion-and-maintenance">Health Promotion and Maintenance</a></span><span class="mbt"><i style="left:28.6%;width:28.6%"></i><i class="lo" style="width:28.6%"></i></span><span class="mbv">6–12%</span></div><div class="mb"><span class="mbn"><a href="/nclex-practice-questions/psychosocial-integrity">Psychosocial Integrity</a></span><span class="mbt"><i style="left:28.6%;width:28.6%"></i><i class="lo" style="width:28.6%"></i></span><span class="mbv">6–12%</span></div><div class="mb"><span class="mbn"><a href="/nclex-practice-questions/basic-care-and-comfort">Basic Care and Comfort</a></span><span class="mbt"><i style="left:28.6%;width:28.6%"></i><i class="lo" style="width:28.6%"></i></span><span class="mbv">6–12%</span></div></div><p class="mocs">Solid = minimum, light = maximum (2026 test plan).</p>
      <div class="mocg"><div><b>1 in 5 questions</b><p>About 13–18 on an 85-question exam.</p></div><div><b>It shows up everywhere</b><p>Who first? Who does it? <a href="/next-generation-nclex">NGN case studies</a> ask the same thing.</p></div><div><b>It's the real job</b><p>Prioritize, delegate, hand off, advocate. Every shift. New for 2026: unbiased care<sup><a href="#moc-src-1">[1]</a></sup>.</p></div></div></section><h2>What this category covers</h2><p>Management of Care is one of the eight client needs categories in the NCSBN NCLEX-RN test plan. Expect questions on Prioritization, Delegation, Informed consent, Advance directives, HIPAA, and Ethics.</p>
      <div class="tips"><b>How to study Management of Care</b><ul><li>Work every 'who first' item through the same ladder: airway, breathing, circulation; then unstable before stable, acute before chronic, actual before potential.</li><li>Delegation: the RN keeps initial assessment, care planning, teaching, evaluation, and any unstable client. LPNs take stable, predictable clients. Assistive personnel take routine tasks such as vital signs on stable clients, hygiene, feeding without swallowing risk, and ambulation.</li><li>Know the legal set cold: who explains a procedure vs. who witnesses consent, advance directives and proxies, restraint orders, leaving against medical advice, HIPAA, and mandatory reporting.</li><li>After each prioritization question, say out loud why each of the other clients can safely wait. If you can't, you guessed.</li></ul></div>
      <h2>Free Management of Care practice questions</h2><div class="v26-qw"><div class="v26-qn"><span>Swipe for the next question</span><div><button type="button" class="v26-qp" aria-label="Previous question">‹</button><button type="button" class="v26-qx" aria-label="Next question">›</button></div></div><div class="v26-q" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Practice questions, swipe for the next one"><article class="q" data-t="mc" id="moc4-009">
     <div class="meta">Management of Care · Multiple choice · Generate solutions</div>
     <p class="stem">Which client care task can the RN delegate to an LPN?</p><ol><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-009"> <span><b>A.</b> Giving the first dose of IV vancomycin to a newly admitted client</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-009"> <span><b>B.</b> Triaging clients who walk into the clinic</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-009"> <span><b>C.</b> Developing the plan of care for a client with new heart failure</span></label></li><li data-c="1"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-009"> <span><b>D.</b> Administering a scheduled oral antibiotic to a stable client</span></label></li></ol>
     <button class="btn chk" type="button">Check answer</button><p class="res" aria-live="polite"></p>
     <details><summary>Show answer and rationale</summary><p class="ans">Correct answer: D</p><p>LPNs can give scheduled medications to stable clients. First-dose IV drugs for new admissions, care planning, and triage require RN assessment and judgment.</p><p class="src">Source: NCSBN. Model Nursing Practice Act; state LPN scope of practice</p></details>
     </article><article class="q" data-t="mc" id="moc4-004">
     <div class="meta">Management of Care · Multiple choice · Prioritize hypotheses</div>
     <p class="stem">Which client should the nurse in the psychiatric unit see first?</p><ol><li data-c="1"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-004"> <span><b>A.</b> A client who says the voices are telling him to hurt his roommate</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-004"> <span><b>B.</b> A client who refuses to attend group therapy</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-004"> <span><b>C.</b> A client with depression who is tearful after a phone call</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-004"> <span><b>D.</b> A client asking for a snack</span></label></li></ol>
     <button class="btn chk" type="button">Check answer</button><p class="res" aria-live="polite"></p>
     <details><summary>Show answer and rationale</summary><p class="ans">Correct answer: A</p><p>Command hallucinations directing harm to others are a safety emergency. The other clients have needs but no immediate danger.</p><p class="src">Source: Varcarolis' Foundations of Psychiatric-Mental Health Nursing, 10th ed.</p></details>
     </article><article class="q" data-t="mc" id="moc4-005">
     <div class="meta">Management of Care · Multiple choice · Prioritize hypotheses</div>
     <p class="stem">Which client should the nurse in a pediatric clinic see first?</p><ol><li data-c="1"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-005"> <span><b>A.</b> A 3-year-old who is drooling, sitting forward, and has muffled speech</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-005"> <span><b>B.</b> A 7-year-old needing a school physical</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-005"> <span><b>C.</b> A 5-year-old with an ear infection and a temperature of 101°F (38.3°C)</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-005"> <span><b>D.</b> A 2-year-old with a diaper rash</span></label></li></ol>
     <button class="btn chk" type="button">Check answer</button><p class="res" aria-live="polite"></p>
     <details><summary>Show answer and rationale</summary><p class="ans">Correct answer: A</p><p>Drooling, tripod positioning, and a muffled voice suggest epiglottitis or another upper airway obstruction, an emergency.</p><p class="src">Source: Hockenberry. Wong's Nursing Care of Infants and Children, 12th ed.</p></details>
     </article><article class="q" data-t="sata" id="moc4-011">
     <div class="meta">Management of Care · Select all that apply · Generate solutions</div>
     <p class="stem">The RN is caring for clients with an LPN and AP. Which tasks are appropriate to delegate to the AP? Select all that apply.</p><ol><li data-c="0"><label><input type="checkbox" name="q-moc4-011"> <span><b>A.</b> Teaching a client to use an insulin pen</span></label></li><li data-c="1"><label><input type="checkbox" name="q-moc4-011"> <span><b>B.</b> Helping a client with a hip fracture use the bedpan</span></label></li><li data-c="1"><label><input type="checkbox" name="q-moc4-011"> <span><b>C.</b> Recording a client's food intake</span></label></li><li data-c="1"><label><input type="checkbox" name="q-moc4-011"> <span><b>D.</b> Measuring vital signs on a stable client after a cholecystectomy</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="checkbox" name="q-moc4-011"> <span><b>E.</b> Monitoring a client who just received the first dose of a new opioid</span></label></li></ol>
     <button class="btn chk" type="button">Check answer</button><p class="res" aria-live="polite"></p>
     <details><summary>Show answer and rationale</summary><p class="ans">Correct answers: B, C, D</p><p>Routine measurements, toileting help, and recording intake are within the AP role for stable clients. Monitoring response to a first opioid dose and teaching require nursing assessment.</p><p class="src">Source: NCSBN &amp; ANA. National Guidelines for Nursing Delegation (2019)</p></details>
     </article><article class="q" data-t="mc" id="moc4-019">
     <div class="meta">Management of Care · Multiple choice · Analyze cues</div>
     <p class="stem">Which event is considered a sentinel event?</p><ol><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-019"> <span><b>A.</b> A client's IV infiltrates without injury</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-019"> <span><b>B.</b> A client has mild nausea after a new medication</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-019"> <span><b>C.</b> A client refuses breakfast</span></label></li><li data-c="1"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-019"> <span><b>D.</b> A client dies after receiving an incompatible blood transfusion</span></label></li></ol>
     <button class="btn chk" type="button">Check answer</button><p class="res" aria-live="polite"></p>
     <details><summary>Show answer and rationale</summary><p class="ans">Correct answer: D</p><p>A sentinel event is a client safety event resulting in death, permanent harm, or severe temporary harm. Hemolytic transfusion reactions involving major blood group incompatibility are on The Joint Commission list.</p><p class="src">Source: The Joint Commission. Sentinel Event Policy and Procedures</p></details>
     </article><article class="q" data-t="mc" id="moc4-006">
     <div class="meta">Management of Care · Multiple choice · Prioritize hypotheses</div>
     <p class="stem">Which client in a long-term care facility should the nurse see first?</p><ol><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-006"> <span><b>A.</b> A resident whose family wants an update on weight</span></label></li><li data-c="1"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-006"> <span><b>B.</b> A resident with a new onset of confusion and a temperature of 100.8°F (38.2°C)</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-006"> <span><b>C.</b> A resident who wants to change rooms</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-006"> <span><b>D.</b> A resident with chronic knee pain asking for a scheduled analgesic</span></label></li></ol>
     <button class="btn chk" type="button">Check answer</button><p class="res" aria-live="polite"></p>
     <details><summary>Show answer and rationale</summary><p class="ans">Correct answer: B</p><p>Acute confusion with fever in an older adult may signal sepsis or another acute illness and needs prompt assessment.</p><p class="src">Source: Lewis's Medical-Surgical Nursing, 13th ed. (older adults)</p></details>
     </article><article class="q" data-t="mc" id="moc4-018">
     <div class="meta">Management of Care · Multiple choice · Analyze cues</div>
     <p class="stem">Under Medicare, which client is most likely to qualify for home health services?</p><ol><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-018"> <span><b>A.</b> A client who needs only meal delivery</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-018"> <span><b>B.</b> A client who needs only transportation to appointments</span></label></li><li data-c="1"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-018"> <span><b>C.</b> A homebound client who needs skilled nursing for wound care</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-018"> <span><b>D.</b> A client who drives to work daily and wants help with cleaning</span></label></li></ol>
     <button class="btn chk" type="button">Check answer</button><p class="res" aria-live="polite"></p>
     <details><summary>Show answer and rationale</summary><p class="ans">Correct answer: C</p><p>Medicare home health requires that the client be homebound and need intermittent skilled services such as nursing or therapy under a plan of care.</p><p class="src">Source: CMS. Medicare Home Health Services</p></details>
     </article><article class="q" data-t="mc" id="moc4-007">
     <div class="meta">Management of Care · Multiple choice · Prioritize hypotheses</div>
     <p class="stem">Four clients have new lab results. Which result requires immediate action?</p><ol><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-007"> <span><b>A.</b> Cholesterol of 238 mg/dL in a client on a statin</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-007"> <span><b>B.</b> INR of 2.6 in a client taking warfarin for atrial fibrillation</span></label></li><li data-c="1"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-007"> <span><b>C.</b> Glucose of 42 mg/dL in a client receiving insulin</span></label></li><li data-c="0"><label><input type="radio" name="q-moc4-007"> <span><b>D.</b> Hemoglobin A1C of 7.8% in a client with type 2 diabetes</span></label></li></ol>
     <button class="btn chk" type="button">Check answer</button><p class="res" aria-live="polite"></p>
     <details><summary>Show answer and rationale</summary><p class="ans">Correct answer: C</p><p>Severe hypoglycemia can cause seizures and brain injury and needs immediate treatment. The others need follow-up but aren't emergencies; an INR of 2.6 is therapeutic for atrial fibrillation.</p><p class="src">Source: ADA. Standards of Care in Diabetes, Section 6 (hypoglycemia)</p></details>
     </article>
      </div></div><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/app#practice/MOC">Practice more Management of Care questions</a><a class="btn alt" href="/free-nclex-practice-exam">Take the full practice exam</a></div><div class="split rev"><div class="st"><h2>See your Management of Care score after a full exam</h2><p>The full adaptive practice exam runs 85 to 150 items on a five-hour clock and stops by the same rules as the NCLEX. Results break down by all 8 client needs categories, with a pass-likelihood estimate, so students know exactly what to study next. It's free for every nursing student with an account, with or without a school.</p><p><a href="/free-nclex-practice-exam">The full practice exam</a></p></div><figure class="shot"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span><svg viewBox="0 0 12 14" width="9" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6V4.2a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="1.5" y="6" width="9" height="7" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>vexcura.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/exam-results-cats-1000.webp" srcset="/img/exam-results-cats-1600.webp 1600w, /img/exam-results-cats-1000.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 32px), 720px" width="1000" height="625" alt="Full practice exam results by NCLEX client needs category, from below to above the passing standard" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div><figcaption>Full-exam results by client needs category. Demo student.</figcaption></figure></div><section class="mocf" id="if-you-did-not-pass"><h2>Didn't pass?</h2><p>Check your Candidate Performance Report<sup><a href="#moc-src-3">[3]</a></sup>. If Management of Care says <b>Near</b> or <b>Below</b>, start here. It's the biggest category, so it's worth the most study time.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/nclex-prioritization-questions">Prioritization questions</a><a class="btn alt" href="/study-guides/prioritization-and-delegation">Delegation guide</a></div></section><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><h3>Is Management of Care the largest NCLEX-RN category?</h3><p>Yes. It's 15% to 21% of the exam in the 2026 test plan, the highest of the 8 categories.</p><h3>How many Management of Care questions are on the NCLEX-RN?</h3><p>About 13 to 18 on an 85-question exam, and about 23 to 32 on a 150-question exam.</p><h3>Is it the most failed NCLEX category?</h3><p>No one knows for sure. NCSBN doesn't publish failure rates by category. It is the largest category, so it deserves the most study time.</p><h3>What does it cover?</h3><p>Prioritizing, delegation, assignment, advocacy, handoffs, teamwork, referrals, consent, advance directives, confidentiality, and legal and ethical rights.</p></div><h2>Sources</h2><ol class="mocs"><li id="moc-src-1">NCSBN. 2026 NCLEX-RN Test Plan (effective April 1, 2026 to March 31, 2029). Management of Care: 15% to 21% of items. <a href="https://www.ncsbn.org/exams/testplans.page" rel="noopener">www.ncsbn.org/exams/testplans.page</a></li><li id="moc-src-2">NCSBN. Exams update, 2025 Annual Meeting: 2023 and 2026 NCLEX-RN test plan comparison. <a href="https://www.ncsbn.org/public-files/presentations/2025am_exams-update.pdf" rel="noopener">www.ncsbn.org/public-files/presentations/2025am_exams-update.pdf</a></li><li id="moc-src-3">NCSBN. Sample NCLEX-RN Candidate Performance Report. <a href="https://www.nclex.com/files/2023%20CPR%20Sample%20RN%20111623.pdf" rel="noopener">www.nclex.com/files/2023 CPR Sample RN 111623.pdf</a></li></ol><p class="mocs">Reviewed November 2026.</p><h2>Other NCLEX categories</h2><div class="grid"><a class="card" href="/nclex-practice-questions/safety-and-infection-control"><b>Safety and Infection Prevention and Control</b><small>10–16% of the exam</small></a><a class="card" href="/nclex-practice-questions/health-promotion-and-maintenance"><b>Health Promotion and Maintenance</b><small>6–12% of the exam</small></a><a class="card" href="/nclex-practice-questions/psychosocial-integrity"><b>Psychosocial Integrity</b><small>6–12% of the exam</small></a><a class="card" href="/nclex-practice-questions/basic-care-and-comfort"><b>Basic Care and Comfort</b><small>6–12% of the exam</small></a><a class="card" href="/nclex-practice-questions/pharmacology"><b>Pharmacological and Parenteral Therapies</b><small>13–19% of the exam</small></a><a class="card" href="/nclex-practice-questions/reduction-of-risk-potential"><b>Reduction of Risk Potential</b><small>9–15% of the exam</small></a><a class="card" href="/nclex-practice-questions/physiological-adaptation"><b>Physiological Adaptation</b><small>11–17% of the exam</small></a></div><h2>Related</h2><ul class="rel"><li><a href="/free-nclex-practice-exam">Full adaptive NCLEX-RN practice exam</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-prioritization-questions">NCLEX prioritization questions</a></li><li><a href="/next-generation-nclex">Next Generation NCLEX (NGN) guide</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-study-guides">Free NCLEX study guides (PDF)</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-pass-guarantee">NCLEX pass guarantee: registration fee back if you qualify and don't pass</a></li></ul></div><section class="band vxs-band"><div class="vxs-bg" data-vxs-i="0" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="vxs-sh" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="w"><h2>Free for every nursing student</h2><p>Create an account and get the full adaptive NCLEX-RN practice exam, 1,220 cited questions, 8 NGN case studies, the Epic-style academic EHR and the simulations, with or without a school. Nursing programs license Vexcura for their cohorts and faculty, and every plan includes everything.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/app#signup" data-cta="band">Create your free account</a><a class="btn alt" href="/for-nursing-schools">For nursing schools</a></div></div></section></main><footer class="foot mktf"><div class="w">
